From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Open Video Tools contributors <noreply@ovt.dev>
Date: 2026-11-16
Subject: [PATCH] Keep PU/TU syntax and CU/CTB bit positions

Extends the DE265_INTERNALS build (patch 0001) with an opt-in store of the syntax elements
that the decoder reads and then drops. A decoder context with
de265_internals_set_parameter_bool(ctx, DE265_INTERNALS_PARAM_KEEP_SYNTAX, 1) keeps, for
every picture it starts afterwards:

  - per 4x4, the prediction-unit syntax as signalled (merge_flag, merge_idx, inter_pred_idc,
    ref_idx_lX, mvp_lX_flag, MvdLX; prev_intra_luma_pred_flag, mpm_idx,
    rem_intra_luma_pred_mode, intra_chroma_pred_mode), written in read_prediction_unit(),
    read_prediction_unit_SKIP() and the intra branch of read_coding_unit(),
  - per 4x4, the transform-unit syntax (cbf_luma/cb/cr, transform_skip_flag,
    explicit_rdpcm_flag/dir, LastSignificantCoeffX/Y, the number of non-zero coefficients,
    cu_qp_delta_abs/sign, cu_chroma_qp_offset_flag/idx), gathered in residual_coding() and
    written at the end of read_transform_unit(),
  - the entropy-coded size of every coding unit (start to end of coding_unit()) and of every
    CTB (end of the previous CTB to the end of coding_tree_unit() and
    end_of_slice_segment_flag), in 1/8 bits from the CABAC decoder position. The last CTB of
    a substream or slice segment also takes the end_of_subset_one_bit, the byte alignment and
    the bits up to rbsp_slice_segment_trailing_bits, so that the CTBs of a slice segment add
    up to its slice_segment_data() size exactly, with and without worker threads.

They are read with de265_internals_get_PU_syntax(), _get_TU_syntax(), _get_CU_bits_x8() and
_get_CTB_bits_x8(). With KEEP_SYNTAX off nothing is allocated and each write point is one
pointer test; decoded pictures are identical with it on and off.

All new functions have C linkage and the de265_internals_ prefix (the internal ones are
declared in de265_internals_syntax.h, not installed), so the ON library still adds only
de265_internals_* symbols; every change is compiled only when DE265_INTERNALS is defined, so
the OFF library stays identical to upstream. Every modified upstream file carries a dated
modification notice (GPL-3.0 section 5(a), through LGPL-3.0); the new header is
LGPL-3.0-or-later like libde265.

Upstream-Status: Pending [to be offered to strukturag/libde265 after patch 0001, WI-2.167]
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 The Open Video Tools contributors
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-3.0-or-later
Rationale: merge/AMVP choices, motion vector differences, per-component cbf, transform skip,
  coefficient counts and bit positions exist only transiently inside slice.cc (chapter 07
  section 7.6.2, patch 0002).
